  "checked_against_source": true,
  "note": "Components of the compliance contribution tensor of a pore bounded by |x1|^(2p) + |x2|^(2p) + |x3/gamma|^(2p) = 1 (Eq. 1.1), with the normalization of Eq. (2.1): extra strain = (V*/V) H : stress, V* the volume of the pore. The values are dimensionless. The article does not state the factor in the text read; at p = 1 and gamma = 1 they equal E0 H of a spherical pore for a Poisson ratio of the matrix 0.3 to within 0.05 %, and the article gives nu0 = 0.30 for its Section 4. The components H1122 and H1133 are printed with a minus sign in the header, i.e. the tables give -H1122 and -H1133; they are stored here with their sign. The table of H1133 is printed with seven columns, gamma = 0.2 to 5.0: it has no column gamma = 0.1. The pore of this article has three separate exponents: it is axisymmetric for p = 1 only, and for gamma = 1 it is the supersphere."
 },
